from pathlib import Path
import json,html
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;out=R/'data/activity_comparison';r=json.loads((out/'report.json').read_text());names=list(r['summary']);fields=['Water','Dry fuel','Fuel-gas release'];chunks=[]
for phase,title in [('active','Substantially active throughout'),('transition','Crosses activity categories'),('weak','Weak residual change throughout'),('quiet','Quiet throughout')]:
 n=r['counts'][phase];body=f'<section id="{phase}"><h2>{title}</h2><p>{n:,} forecasts · {100*n/r["counts"]["all"]:.1f}% of sampled forecasts. Counts include replicas; errors use balanced configurations and folds.</p>'
 for metric,heading,explain in [('error_vs_sim_percent','1. Error relative to the simulation','Lower is better. Average absolute error divided by the average absolute simulated value.'),('reduction_vs_no_change_percent','2. Improvement over holding the starting state constant','Higher is better. Positive = less error than no change. Negative = more error than no change.')]:
  body+=f'<h3>{heading}</h3><p>{explain}</p><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th>'+''.join(f'<th>{x}</th>' for x in fields)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'
  for name in names:
   values=r['summary'][name][phase][metric][:3];body+='<tr><th>'+name+'</th>'+''.join(f'<td>{v:,.2f}%</td>' for v in values)+'</tr>'
  body+='<tr class="missing"><th>4-state MLP</th><td colspan="3">Not trained — no result available</td></tr></tbody></table>'
 body+='<h3>3. Absolute error, for scale</h3><p>All values below are in grams or grams per second. Lower is better. This is especially important when gas release is almost zero.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Water (g)</th><th>Dry fuel (g)</th><th>Gas release (g/s)</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
 for name in names+['Hold starting state constant']:
  values=r['summary'][names[0] if name=='Hold starting state constant' else name][phase]['no_change_mae' if name=='Hold starting state constant' else 'model_mae'][:3];body+='<tr><th>'+name+'</th>'+''.join(f'<td>{v*1000:,.3f}</td>' for v in values)+'</tr>'
 body+='</tbody></table>'
 if phase!='active':body+='<p class="note">Gas release is very small in this group. Its percentage error can be enormous even for a small absolute error. Do not interpret it without the grams/second table.</p>'
 body+='</section>';chunks.append(body)
page='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>16-second fire-state forecasts</title><style>body{font:18px/1.5 system-ui;background:#f5f7fa;color:#142231;margin:0}main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:36px}h1{font-size:34px}h2{font-size:27px;margin-top:0}h3{margin-top:32px}p{max-width:900px}nav{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;position:sticky;top:0;background:#f5f7fa;padding:12px 0}button{font:inherit;padding:10px 16px;border:1px solid #b4bfcd;border-radius:8px;background:white;cursor:pointer}button.selected{background:#123b5e;color:white}section{background:white;padding:28px;border-radius:12px;margin-top:16px}section:not(.shown){display:none}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}td,th{padding:14px;border-bottom:1px solid #d4dce6;text-align:right}th:first-child{text-align:left}thead{background:#eaf0f6}.missing{color:#677584}.note{padding:16px;background:#fff1d7;border-left:4px solid #ad6b00}footer{margin-top:28px;font-size:15px;color:#46566a}</style><main><h1>How well do the models predict 16 seconds ahead?</h1><p><b>Three measured comparisons. No four-state MLP was trained.</b><br>Three-state models predict water, dry fuel and vegetation fuel-gas release. The four-state GRU also predicts a surface-heating index—not heat energy.</p><p>Each forecast starts from observed history and then uses its own predictions for eight two-second steps. These are test-fold averages, grouped by the simulation’s activity over that whole forecast interval.</p><nav>'''
for phase,label in [('active','Active'),('transition','Transitions'),('weak','Weak residual'),('quiet','Quiet')]:page+=f'<button onclick="show(\'{phase}\')" data-tab="{phase}">{label}</button>'
page+='</nav>'+''.join(chunks)+'''<footer><b>Activity definition:</b> trailing nominal10seconds, ≥0.1% initial dry-fuel-equivalent release or initial water loss per10seconds. Quiet: both below0.01%. Intermediate rates are weak residual. Every forecast step must share the category to count as stable; otherwise it is a transition. Active includes drying, not necessarily combustion. Trailing smoothing delays labels. Thresholds are engineering tolerances, not physically validated extinction criteria.<p>Equal mean across available test folds, with configurations and replicas balanced inside each fold. Same520histories/480configurations; historically examined and reshuffled test data. Separate experiments combine architecture and state changes; not a full factorial controlled study. Local inference only; whole-history error replay agreed with saved GPU results within0.3%.</p><p>Generic3m-wide vegetation cones,4/6/8/10m heights above2m,1600weightedparticles,.5m mesh24×16×16m,180s,1500°C20s artificial ignitor; no trunks/buildings/embers.48legacy geometries retained. Fuel-gas yield0.75; char treated as inert ash. No physical validation.</p></footer></main><script>function show(id){document.querySelectorAll('section').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('shown',x.id===id));document.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('selected',x.dataset.tab===id));}show('active')</script>'''
(out/'report.html').write_text(page)
